#0--------#10-------#20-------#30-------#40-------#50-------#60-------#70-------
hscroll-fps 10000
title-x 0
title-y 0
title-width 0
title-height 1
content-x 2
content-y 2
content-width 0
content-height -2
terminal-minimum-height 24
terminal-minimum-width 80
!CONTENT!
!label 0,-1 asciiSHOW by SYSAU LAB
!label -1,-1 lab.sysau.com
!label c,c Introduction to asciiSHOW
!slide Welcome to the asciiSHOW tutorial
Are you tired of having to choose fonts, colors and graphics 
for your presentations?

Look no further, asciiSHOW do not features any of this nonsense.
asciiSHOW is text based only and do not support color.

Now you can finally focus on your content 
instead of being anxious about your graphics and layout!

How does it work you ask?
Press any key to go to the next slide and discover its magic!
#
#
#
!center
!slide A FEW FACTS
The slides are easy to edit text files, no editor required.

It is written in python3 and should work pretty much anywhere.

To view your presentation, type:
python3 asciishow.py your_presentation.txt

To view this demo, type:
python3 asciishow.py

ADVISORIES

Do NOT resize your terminal during a presentation.
Do NOT write more text lines in content areas, it will crash.
Do NOT insert content before declaring a first slide.
#
#
#
!right
!slide FILE FORMAT
COMMENTS
Every lines STARTING by # are completely ignored
To demonstrate the examples, the lines are indented by two spaces

Exemple:
  #this line start with a #, is a comment
   #this line start with a space, not a comment
  This is content #this is still content, not a comment
#
#
#
!left
!slide
GENERAL LAYOUT

A presentation file contains 2 sections:
- The configuration
- The content

The two sections are seperated by a single containing !CONTENT!

Exemple:
  settings 1
  settings 2
  settings 3
  !CONTENT!
  !slide 1
  bla bla bla 
  content
#
#
#
!slide SETTINGS
The configuration is done by named key-pair. 
The parser look for the name of the setting at the beggining of the line.
The line is split between white spaces, the block following the name 
is considered the setting and the rest is ignored.

Example:
  name setting can be used for comments ONLY in configuration
#
#
#
!slide
All the settings availables and their default setting
This is a valid configuration file, composed of name at the beginning 
of the line, a value and the rest is ignored.

  hscroll-fps 100              The speed characters are written
  title-x 2                    The horizontal position of title box
  title-y 1                    The vertical position of title box
  title-width -2               Width of the title box
  title-height 1               Height of the title box
  content-x 4                  The horizontal position of content box
  content-y 3                  The vertical position of content box
  content-width 0              Width of the content box
  content-height -2            Height of the content box
  terminal-minimum-height 24   Minimum height required for presentation
  terminal-minimum-width 80    Minimum width required for presentation
#
#
#
!slide SETTINGS: hscroll-fps
Accepted values : integer >= 1 

This could aslo be named baud. It controls the rate at which content 
and title characters appears on screenaccording to the formula:

(1 / hscroll-fps) seconds

Examples:
  10: 8 seconds to fill a complete line of standard terminal.
  100: .8 seconds to fill a complete line of standard terminal.
  300: Mimics the speed of the first modems...

Just play with it until you find your sweet spot :-)
#
#
#
!slide SETTINGS: box-x AND box-y
Here "box-x" refer to both title-x and content-x... or y.
Substitute box according to your needs.

The title and content box are positionned relative to the 
top left corner of the terminal. The values accepted are positive integer.
(0, 1, 2, 3, etc)

Please make sure your boxes do not exceed the geometry of the terminal.
If you do, it will crash the program.
#
#
#
!slide SETTINGS: box-x AND box-y, EXAMPLES
box-x 0
box-y 0
